  {
   "id": "crush-operators-md-8",
   "kind": {
    "type": "markdown"
   },
   "source": "Conditions in `if`/`while` must be `Bool` — see [Types](https://docs.crushlang.org/crush/types.html#conditions-must-be-bool).\n\n## Range\n\n`a..b` is a half-open range (`a` inclusive, `b` exclusive). It is used by `for`,\nand also evaluates to an array of the integers in the range:\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "done"
   },
   "meta": {},
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "id": "crush-operators-5",
   "kind": {
    "type": "crush"
   },
   "source": "for i in 2..5 {\n    print(i)\n}\nlet r = 1..5\nprint(r)\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "pending"
   },
   "meta": {
    "tags": [
     "guide",
     "runnable"
    ],
    "extra": {
     "guide": {
      "src": "crush/operators.md:109",
      "browser": "run",
      "expect_output": "2\n3\n4\n[1, 2, 3, 4]\n"
     }
    }
   },
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "id": "crush-operators-md-10",
   "kind": {
    "type": "markdown"
   },
   "source": "An empty or reversed range (`5..2`) produces no iterations. Both bounds may be\nexpressions: `for i in 0..len(items)`. There is no `range()` function.\n\n## Pipeline\n\n`x |> f` calls `f(x)`; `x |> f(y)` calls `f(x, y)`. Chains read left to right.\nThe right side must be a user-defined function (or a call to one):\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "done"
   },
   "meta": {},
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "id": "crush-operators-6",
   "kind": {
    "type": "crush"
   },
   "source": "fn inc(x) {\n    return x + 1\n}\nfn dbl(x) {\n    return x * 2\n}\nfn add(a, b) {\n    return a + b\n}\n\nprint(3 |> inc |> dbl)\nprint(3 |> add(4))\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "pending"
   },
   "meta": {
    "tags": [
     "guide",
     "runnable"
    ],
    "extra": {
     "guide": {
      "src": "crush/operators.md:133",
      "browser": "run",
      "expect_output": "8\n7\n"
     }
    }
   },
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "id": "crush-operators-md-12",
   "kind": {
    "type": "markdown"
   },
   "source": "Piping into a **capability** such as `str.trim` or `conv.to_str` is rejected\n(`Pipeline right side must be function`); wrap it in a function first:\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "done"
   },
   "meta": {},
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "id": "crush-operators-7",
   "kind": {
    "type": "crush"
   },
   "source": "fn main() {\n    print(\"  hi  \" |> str.trim)\n}\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "pending"
   },
   "meta": {
    "tags": [
