  {
   "id": "crush-operators-md-14",
   "kind": {
    "type": "markdown"
   },
   "source": "## Not available\n\nBitwise operators (`&`, `|`, `^`, `~`, `<<`, `>>`) are **not** part of the\nCrush language today — the lexer rejects them — even though CASM has `bit_*`\nopcodes ([CASM reference](https://docs.crushlang.org/casm/instructions.html)). There is no ternary\n`a ? b : c`, no null-coalescing `??`, and no `**`.\n\n## Precedence (high → low)\n\n| Level | Operators |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | `()`, `.`, `[]` — call, field access, indexing |\n| 2 | unary `-`, `!` |\n| 3 | `*` `/` `%` |\n| 4 | `+` `-` |\n| 5 | `<` `>` `<=` `>=` |\n| 6 | `==` `!=` |\n| 7 | `&&` |\n| 8 | `\\|\\|` |\n| 9 | `\\|>` |\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "done"
   },
   "meta": {},
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "id": "crush-operators-8",
   "kind": {
    "type": "crush"
   },
   "source": "print(2 + 3 * 4)\nprint((2 + 3) * 4)\nprint(1 + 1 == 2 && 2 * 2 == 4)\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "pending"
   },
